lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={82.87}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+{82.87}^{∘}={262.87}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are\n\n$$\nx={83}^{∘},{263}^{∘}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092569 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71da663-e7a4-5781-973c-5dc7e4deb83f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points of Intersection of a Horizontal Line and a Tangent Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa391f15-ed79-503c-8853-6a934916a3a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5π}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089963} {:answer/id #uuid "ae0d4b5d-44f0-5d56-bcd2-fb5262721c9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3π}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089964} {:answer/id #uuid "cdd09b7a-a563-5a5f-b874-f817c83ba70a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5π}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089965} {:answer/id #uuid "e0bc28a2-7a1c-562d-a2a8-1bfa85a54dd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2π}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089966} {:answer/id #uuid "745711e3-0785-5533-b4bc-cf0ce9b36e22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7π}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa391f15-ed79-503c-8853-6a934916a3a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5π}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089963} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e120544-bc70-5902-af42-e303b9ccd721" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fc963679-7e9a-589a-a899-b98503fae964" :question/math-academy-id "q-20414" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040762/assets/f00d8bd6cbd1f113df7f023e161e4d79e2f4a81157d1ac9a8ab65e70b4959221.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.$  Find the $x$-coordinate of the point $B.$" :question/worked-solution "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n$$\n\n Now, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis value lies inside $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi $ hence, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ This is the $x$ coordinate of $A.$\n\nTo get another solution, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Thus,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +x=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $B$ is $\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310815 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebf8592e-1a43-5d65-af3c-9becd79ae8b9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73e909f5-78ee-53fe-bb18-bede70ec9494" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73e909f5-78ee-53fe-bb18-bede70ec9494" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310817} :answer-field/id #uuid "445054b9-825a-5ce0-b82b-ff86e3dd2d9d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310816} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9070e76c-7a27-5852-9983-b8430eef8d6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9070e76c-7a27-5852-9983-b8430eef8d6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310819} :answer-field/id #uuid "c07805b2-10ab-579e-b77b-512c5b8c8ed1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310818}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9a84cfd7-c56d-5efb-9a8c-2be7100fb694" :question/math-academy-id "q-321873" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in degrees** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=0$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)={0}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${0}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={0}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+{x}_{1}={180}^{∘}+{0}^{∘}={180}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=0\\,{\\,}^{∘}$ and $x=180\\,{\\,}^{∘}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310820 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71da663-e7a4-5781-973c-5dc7e4deb83f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points of Intersection of a Horizontal Line and a Tangent Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06e44d1c-5727-574f-9456-55f484edbf7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310822} {:answer/id #uuid "fccff7b1-4756-5608-8f85-48242f7d6791" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310823} {:answer/id #uuid "753265bd-6bc0-55f9-b310-90be13f48324" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310824} {:answer/id #uuid "b3f9d6e7-dc7d-5361-a47a-0f41e590fc34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310825} {:answer/id #uuid "c535e997-0a1b-5a3b-9de6-388f4be826fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "753265bd-6bc0-55f9-b310-90be13f48324" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310824} :answer-field/id #uuid "337be623-0765-5208-8fa1-c7a6844e7598" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310821}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5d62320a-16d8-5d65-a5c8-38ba023de3aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-72829" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040762/assets/6e2223a7dadd9aeddad0b029bf2ba8fc18bafc74dcaca88346ee2b702029b597.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=-\\sqrt{3}.$  Find the $x$-coordinate of the point $B.$" :question/worked-solution "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis value lies inside $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi $, hence, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ This is the $x$ coordinate of $A.$\n\nTo get another solution, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Thus,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +x=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $B$ is  $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310827 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebf8592e-1a43-5d65-af3c-9becd79ae8b9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c82aa5d-5695-5d50-86c8-39ff01f155a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310829} {:answer/id #uuid "a1888ab6-0098-537d-85f7-0211ab7a9ebf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310830} {:answer/id #uuid "91491e93-ade1-57e8-9f23-74678e6688cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310831} {:answer/id #uuid "19eb3c5d-3e30-5446-ab7c-8819593de153" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310832} {:answer/id #uuid "269a72b7-e3cc-5167-ad3f-5f483db9ec7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "269a72b7-e3cc-5167-ad3f-5f483db9ec7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310833} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffee3412-680e-5443-a8c2-be99a34bf665" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "83c4983f-27a4-5a4b-a144-f5f68c5b2962" :question/math-academy-id "q-8715" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $0$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=0.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=\\pi +{x}_{1}=\\pi +0=\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=0,\\pi .$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=0\\cdot \\pi =0.\n$$"}]}
